WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:17.108
Two members of the submarine's crew helped us to dress for our underwater walk.

2
00:00:18.009 --> 00:00:23.252
Our diving suits were made of heavy rubber and constructed to resist the great pressure of the water.

3
00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:29.756
Each suit consisted of a jacket and trousers joined together with bands of copper crossing the chest.

4
00:00:30.592 --> 00:00:33.854
The sleeves ended in gloves that allowed the fingers to move easily.

5
00:00:34.755 --> 00:00:38.537
The trousers were finished off with thick boots weighted with heavy lead.

6
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:43.461
Captain Nemo, one of his crew, Conseil, and I were soon dressed.

7
00:00:44.341 --> 00:00:49.065
The upper part of the diving suit ended in a copper collar upon which was screwed a metal

8
00:00:49.125 --> 00:00:54.808
helmet. Three holes, protected by thick glass, allowed us to see in all directions.

9
00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:59.892
I was relieved to find that I could breathe with ease once the apparatus was turned on.

10
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:04.267
Our diving suits were so heavy that it was difficult to walk.

11
00:01:05.187 --> 00:01:08.830
Fortunately we only had to take a few steps into another small room.

12
00:01:09.811 --> 00:01:13.854
Then the door closed and we were wrapped in profound darkness.

13
00:01:14.915 --> 00:01:20.260
After a few minutes, I heard a loud hissing and felt cold rising from my feet to my

14
00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:23.242
chest. Evidently water was entering the room.

15
00:01:24.243 --> 00:01:28.587
When the room was full of water, another door opened in the side of the submarine and we

16
00:01:28.687 --> 00:01:30.088
stepped onto the sea bottom!

17
00:01:31.176 --> 00:01:34.378
How can I explain what it was like to walk underwater?

18
00:01:35.219 --> 00:01:37.000
Mere words are insufficient.

19
00:01:37.861 --> 00:01:39.762
I was astonished by how bright it was.

20
00:01:40.743 --> 00:01:44.906
Would you believe me if I said that at a depth of thirty feet I could see as

21
00:01:44.966 --> 00:01:46.027
if in broad daylight?

22
00:01:47.488 --> 00:01:57.875
The sun's rays touched flowers, rocks, plants, and shells, providing a perfect kaleidoscope of colors: red, green, yellow,

23
00:01:58.155 --> 00:01:59.356
orange, purple, and blue.

24
00:02:00.308 --> 00:02:05.011
I wanted to share my amazement with Conseil, but underwater there was no way to communicate with him.

25
00:02:06.031 --> 00:02:09.993
Soon the nature of the soil changed from sand to slimy mud.

26
00:02:10.994 --> 00:02:16.137
Then we traveled over a plain of algae that was as soft as any carpet woven by man.

27
00:02:17.198 --> 00:02:20.239
After a while the ground began to slope downward.

28
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:25.222
The colors were no longer as brilliant, but we had no need of our lights yet.

29
00:02:26.122 --> 00:02:31.009
When we reached a depth of about three hundred feet, Captain Nemo signaled for us to stop.

30
00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:34.992
He pointed to a dark mass looming in the shadows.

31
00:02:36.012 --> 00:02:39.854
"This must be the forest of Crespo," I thought and I was right.

32
00:02:41.315 --> 00:02:44.137
As the captain had said, the forest was underwater.

33
00:02:44.937 --> 00:02:46.278
There was no sign of an island.

34
00:02:47.219 --> 00:02:49.620
Captain Nemo regarded this forest as his own.

35
00:02:50.681 --> 00:02:53.943
And who would have challenged his possession of this underwater real estate?

36
00:02:54.803 --> 00:02:59.682
What other pioneer would come, hatchet in hand, to cut down these dark masses of plant life?

37
00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:03.905
The forest was composed of large plants that resembled trees.

38
00:03:04.825 --> 00:03:10.169
I was struck by the unusual position of their branches, something that I had never observed before.

39
00:03:11.169 --> 00:03:16.093
No herb that carpeted the ground or branch that adorned a tree extended horizontally.

40
00:03:16.973 --> 00:03:21.216
They all stretched up to the surface of the ocean as straight as iron bars.

41
00:03:22.224 --> 00:03:26.667
I soon grew used to this strange fact as well as to the growing darkness that surrounded us.

42
00:03:28.048 --> 00:03:33.072
The soil of the forest was covered with sharp rocks that were difficult to avoid, and it was

43
00:03:33.132 --> 00:03:35.073
hard to tell the plants from the animals.

44
00:03:36.114 --> 00:03:41.278
It was still impossible to speak and be heard, so I put my great copper head next to

45
00:03:41.318 --> 00:03:44.360
Conseil's. His eyes were shining with delight.

46
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:50.164
After a couple hours of walking underwater, I was surprised that I wasn't terribly hungry.

47
00:03:51.144 --> 00:03:56.447
Instead I felt an overwhelming desire to sleep, something that happens to all divers.

48
00:03:57.208 --> 00:03:58.748
We all stretched out for a nap.

49
00:03:59.689 --> 00:04:04.412
I don't know how long I stayed asleep, but when I awoke, Captain Nemo had already risen.

50
00:04:05.472 --> 00:04:09.755
I was starting to stretch my limbs when something startled me and I jumped to my feet.

51
00:04:10.755 --> 00:04:18.560
A few steps away a giant sea spider, thirty-eight inches high, was watching me and was ready to

52
00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:25.089
spring. Although my diving suit was thick enough to protect me from this animal, I couldn't help shuddering

53
00:04:25.109 --> 00:04:25.649
with horror.

54
00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:32.011
At this moment Conseil and the other sailor from the Nautilus awoke, and Captain Nemo pointed out the

55
00:04:32.131 --> 00:04:33.111
hideous crustacean.

56
00:04:34.112 --> 00:04:37.793
He knocked the creature over with his gun, and I saw its horrible claws.

57
00:04:38.733 --> 00:04:44.895
This incident made me aware that we might encounter even more fearful animals—creatures whose attacks might penetrate my

58
00:04:44.935 --> 00:04:45.515
diving suit.

59
00:04:46.495 --> 00:04:49.516
I hadn't thought of this before, but I resolved to be on my guard.

60
00:04:50.536 --> 00:04:54.659
I was sure that our resting spot would mark the end of our walk, but Captain Nemo pressed

61
00:04:54.799 --> 00:05:01.704
on. We continued going downhill until we reached a depth of 450 feet and it got very dark.

62
00:05:03.245 --> 00:05:08.449
I had no instruments to measure this depth, but I knew that the sun's rays couldn't penetrate even

63
00:05:08.489 --> 00:05:10.711
the clearest water at 450 feet.

64
00:05:11.651 --> 00:05:14.033
We turned on our lights and could see ahead of us.

65
00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:20.853
Captain Nemo kept plunging into the depths of the forest, whose trees were getting scarcer at every step.

66
00:05:21.833 --> 00:05:25.494
I was sure that our lights would draw some deep-sea dweller from its dark bed.

67
00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:29.695
But if sea creatures did approach us, they kept a respectful distance.

68
00:05:30.755 --> 00:05:35.817
Several times Captain Nemo raised his gun to his shoulder, but then dropped it and walked on.

69
00:05:36.877 --> 00:05:42.619
At last this marvelous excursion came to an end when we reached a wall of solid rock.

70
00:05:43.579 --> 00:05:44.619
There was no way to climb it.

71
00:05:45.279 --> 00:05:50.042
We had reached the base of the island of Crespo, and Captain Nemo would not venture onto land.

72
00:05:51.543 --> 00:05:54.345
We returned home by a different, steeper route.

73
00:05:55.326 --> 00:06:00.410
As we reached shallower waters, the captain shot a sea otter and his companion brought down a bird

74
00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:01.712
that was hovering above the waves.

75
00:06:02.712 --> 00:06:07.176
Off in the distance I spotted the bright light from the Nautilus; we would be onboard in less

76
00:06:07.196 --> 00:06:07.837
than twenty minutes.

77
00:06:08.917 --> 00:06:12.040
I could tell that my air supply was beginning to run low on oxygen.

78
00:06:13.041 --> 00:06:16.604
Suddenly Captain Nemo rushed toward me and pushed me to the ground.

79
00:06:17.324 --> 00:06:19.246
His companion did the same thing to Conseil.

80
00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:24.251
I didn't know what to think of this unexpected attack, but I was reassured by seeing the captain

81
00:06:24.291 --> 00:06:26.433
lie down beside me and remain motionless.

82
00:06:27.454 --> 00:06:31.998
I was stretched on the ground just under the shelter of an algae bush when I saw an

83
00:06:32.078 --> 00:06:34.120
enormous mass glide overhead.

84
00:06:35.641 --> 00:06:40.846
My blood froze in my veins as I recognized two giant sharks passing over us.

85
00:06:41.807 --> 00:06:47.888
They were blue sharks—an especially fierce kind of shark that could crush a man with their iron jaws!

86
00:06:48.849 --> 00:06:51.792
Happily for us, these hungry creatures couldn't see well.

87
00:06:52.713 --> 00:06:56.496
They passed without spotting us even though they brushed us with their fins.

88
00:06:57.477 --> 00:07:02.361
By some miracle, we managed to escape a danger greater than meeting a tiger face-to-face!

89
00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:05.644
In a few minutes, we were back at the Nautilus.

90
00:07:06.705 --> 00:07:10.068
I don't know whether Conseil had classified the sharks as they swam over us.

91
00:07:11.036 --> 00:07:16.059
All I know is that I had observed them more as a potential victim than as a naturalist.
